# VALIDATION (2026-10-05/06, one R9700, Qwen3.8-27B MXFP4, DFlash2 x7, fp8 KV, MAXSEQS=2):
#   * GDN scan: against an fp64 sequential recurrence (magiccodingman/vllm-radiance#8
#     check_gdn_extreme_decay), libr4d b9e42ab + rx9 fails 6/12 cases (46-94% output error at chunk gate
#     spans 200-2000); this build passes 12/12 + CUDA-graph replay within 0.36%, fp32 and fp16 state.
#   * DSPLIT: output BIT-IDENTICAL to DS=1 on 10 shapes (q 16-2048, ctx 4k-100k), fp8 QK8+PV8 and f16
#     legs (r4d_kernels/tests/dsplit_bench.py); 1.26-1.42x on final chunks of 64 tokens or fewer.
#   * Lazy GDN (opt-in): concurrent multi-turn soak with a lazy-off control, no lazy-specific failure;
#     ggz14's original corruption was never reproduced, so the mode-2 fix is unproven, not disproven.
#   * Served end to end: cold vs KV-offload resume token-identical (val_resume --evict), 40-minute
#     two-agent soak 0 engine faults. Built from libr4d-rx13 branch rx16 (755db41).
#   * rx17 (2026-10-08): gdn_lazy_materialize no longer requires a stash block when there is nothing to
#     replay (count == 0). Before, mode 0 returned WITHOUT migrating the state when bt[src_col + 1] was
#     null -- which happens when a prefill step spans more than one mamba block and the request resumes
#     from the KV-offload tier -- so the step ran from a stale running block: gross garbage. It is what
#     broke fp16 SSM state (880-token blocks make CHUNK=2048 two blocks per step) and any CHUNK above
#     one block. Fixed: val_resume --evict bit-exact at fp32 CHUNK=4956 and fp16 CHUNK=3532 (rx16:
#     0/8); concurrent deep multi-turn gate (2 in flight, 6 x 70k conversations, ~3M tokens restored
#     from the tier) 48/48 (rx16 control: 7/48). Decode (count > 0) is unchanged.
